# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model endpoint
#
# The application is vendor-neutral. It speaks one wire format — the widely
# implemented chat-completions shape — and knows only a base URL, a key and a
# model name. Any service exposing that format works; see README.md for base
# URLs that are known to work, including free and locally hosted options.
#
# Leave these unset to run with no endpoint at all: the app serves a built-in
# sample paper and written responses are shown with their marking guideline
# instead of a mark.
#
# Check a configuration with:  pnpm ai:smoke
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# An administrator can set all of these on /settings instead, and what is
# saved there wins over anything here.
AI_BASE_URL=
AI_API_KEY=
AI_MODEL=

# Optional per-stage models. Anything unset falls back to AI_MODEL.
# Generating questions can use a cheaper model than marking them, because a
# weak mark on a correct answer costs far more trust than a weak question.
# AI_MODEL_BLUEPRINT=
# AI_MODEL_QUESTION=
# AI_MODEL_CRITIC=
# AI_MODEL_MARKING=
# AI_MODEL_MODERATION=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What the model is used for. These are separate decisions: producing a paper
# is ~100 calls, marking one is ~30 small ones.
#
#   GENERATION_PROVIDER  sample | model   (default: sample)
#   MARKING_PROVIDER     none   | model   (default: model once an endpoint is set)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GENERATION_PROVIDER=sample
# MARKING_PROVIDER=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database — Postgres
#
# `DATABASE_URL` is what the application queries through. On a hosted database
# with connection pooling (Supabase, Neon), use the *pooled* connection string:
# a serverless function opens a connection per invocation, and the pooler is
# what stops that exhausting the database.
#
# `DIRECT_DATABASE_URL` is the unpooled connection, used only by
# `pnpm db:migrate`. A pooler runs in transaction mode, which cannot hold the
# locks and multi-statement DDL a migration needs. On a database without a
# pooler, leave it unset and the migration uses DATABASE_URL.
#
# On Vercel, the Supabase integration injects the same two connections under
# its own names — POSTGRES_URL and POSTGRES_URL_NON_POOLING — and manages them,
# so they cannot be renamed. Both spellings are accepted, these first. Nothing
# needs setting by hand there; a DATABASE_URL left over from before the database
# was provisioned is ignored on a host that could not have used it anyway.
#
# For local development you can point DATABASE_URL at a directory instead of a
# connection string, and it runs PGlite — Postgres compiled to WebAssembly,
# in-process, no server and no network. The test suite always does this.
#
#   hosted   DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:6543/postgres
#            DIRECT_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:5432/postgres
#   local    DATABASE_URL=./data/local-pg
#
# The scripts read this file too, so `pnpm db:migrate` against a hosted
# database needs only the direct connection string here — no exported shell
# variable. What the shell does export always wins over what is written here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
DATABASE_URL=./data/local-pg
# DIRECT_DATABASE_URL=

# Connections per function instance. One is right for a serverless host.
# DATABASE_POOL_MAX=1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Media storage
#
# Uploaded images and video. Left unset, files are written to disk beside the
# database, which works locally and on any host with a persistent volume — but
# not on a serverless host, where the filesystem is read-only and discarded
# between invocations. Set these to keep them in Supabase Storage instead.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SUPABASE_URL=
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
# SUPABASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=exam-media

# Container only: set to `never` to skip corpus ingestion on first start.
# INGEST_ON_START=auto
